# Deny-all. Uploaded .vcf files land here and are read by PHP from disk; HTTP
# must never reach them.
#
# This is the most sensitive directory in the app by some distance. A contacts
# export is names, phone numbers, email addresses and home addresses for
# everyone in somebody's phone, in plain text, under a filename an attacker can
# often guess from the phone's own export naming.
#
# THREE THINGS PROTECT IT, and none of them is trusted alone:
#
#   1. uploads/ sits OUTSIDE public/, so the document-root shim in the root
#      .htaccess never rewrites a request into it.
#   2. lib/import.php deletes the file the moment it has been parsed — the
#      drafts are the artifact, and keeping the raw file means keeping every
#      phone number you decided not to import.
#   3. This file, which needs no modules and no PHP.
#
# 1 lives inside <IfModule mod_rewrite.c> and silently does nothing if the
# module is unavailable. 2 does not happen on the run where the parser threw.
# Same belt-and-braces reasoning as the config.php protection in the root
# .htaccess: the cheap lock is the one that still holds when the clever one
# has quietly stopped working.
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
  Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
  Order allow,deny
  Deny from all
</IfModule>
